.TH mnnn-tui 1  "mnnn-tui 1.12.3" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-tui \- Launch the terminal UI
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn tui\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch the terminal UI
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Everything you can act on is clickable: menus, tiles, sidebar, popup rows, form fields, import picker entries and the key buttons ([X] closes any popup).
.PP
Import (i): pick a file or a whole folder (A imports the folder, recursing). If a symbol cannot be guessed from a file name, a popup asks for it, showing the file name on its own line, its folder below and (file i of n) during folder imports. After an import, if no tile shows data yet, the focused tile loads the first imported series.
.PP
Help (? or F1): follow links with Tab and Enter or a click, Backspace goes back, / searches from any topic; a clickable key bar at the bottom lists the shortcuts.
.PP
Loading: series load in the background; a tile shows a progress bar (bars read of the total) or a spinner while the total is unknown, and the UI stays responsive.
.PP
See mnnn help tui, mnnn help import and mnnn help help.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
